  "result": "Perfect! All 137 tests pass. I've added customer ID normalization to handle mixed-case input with stray spaces:\n\n**Changes to `src/customers.js`:**\n\nAdded `normalizeId(id)` function that:\n- Trims whitespace with `.trim()`\n- Converts to uppercase with `.toUpperCase()`\n- Converts input to string first (handles non-string inputs)\n\nUpdated `getCustomer(id)` to:\n- Normalize the lookup ID before searching\n\n**Changes to `src/invoices.js`:**\n\nUpdated `createInvoice({ customerId, ... })` to:\n- Normalize the incoming customer ID immediately\n- Pass normalized ID to `getCustomer` for validation\n- Store the normalized ID in the invoice object\n\nThis ensures consistency: invoices always contain normalized customer IDs, and all lookups handle various input formats (`'c-001'`, `'C-001'`, `'  C-001  '`, etc.).\n\n**Tests added (8 new, 137 total):**\n\nIn `test/customers.test.js`:\n- `normalizeId` trims whitespace on all sides\n- `normalizeId` converts to uppercase\n- `normalizeId` handles mixed case with spaces\n- `getCustomer` finds customers by lowercase ID\n- `getCustomer` finds customers with spaces\n- `getCustomer` finds customers with both\n\nIn `test/invoices.test.js`:\n- `createInvoice` normalizes incoming customer ID\n- `createInvoice` accepts lowercase customer ID\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Handles mixed-case IDs from upstream systems\n- Strips accidental whitespace\n- Stored invoices have canonical form\n- Lookups work regardless of input format\n\nAll 137 tests pass. \u2705",
